  "$comment": "Per-subpath gzip budgets (plan/21 §1, budget model v2). Keys are export subpaths without './'. Every chart needs an entry — gen-size-limits.mjs fails on a missing one, so adding a chart forces a budget decision. Hard ceilings: static ≤ 3 kB (target 2 kB, Delta-class 1.5 kB), interactive ≤ static + 1 kB. `.size-limit.json` is GENERATED from this file + package.json#exports — never hand-edit it.",
  "$exception": "Sparkline 3.35/4.35 kB was USER-APPROVED (2026-07-08) as a flagship exception to the 3/4 kB hard caps (long-series guard + label=minmax; trims exhausted first — plan/12). Batch 1 W4 raised it to 3.65/4.65 kB PENDING user sign-off at the batch gate: the plan/22 #28 annotations HOST contract adds the children walker + scale frame (~0.29 kB) to every S1/S2 host — the annotation MARK renderers ship in ./annotations (1.46 kB), which consumers import separately, so hosts only pay the walker. Not a precedent for other charts. ANNOTATION-HOST RETROFIT (2026-07-15, USER-APPROVED full value-series family, plan/22 #28): resolveAnnotations walker + scale frame added to 15 value-series hosts. 5 cross the 3 kB static ceiling as approved exceptions (all < Sparkline 3.65): change-point 3.45, win-prob-worm 3.4, forecast-cone/dual-sparkline 3.35, burn-chart 3.25. The other 10 stay < 3 kB.",
